From 2fc8f7ef9f6394e21a566c1e788872772c240b3c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dsh-wake <wake@local>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 02:36:38 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(voice): recognize the utterance instead of streaming it
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The trace settled the streaming path: on the same 20 s of audio the in-app
recognizer wrote 哈哈哈哈 while the same model decoded offline found 小安 at
8.8 s, and a quiet room decoded to nothing offline but to 呵呵呵 in the app. A
streaming model that reaches that state does not leave it, and every reset only
moved the failure.

So the wake path now does what 小安语音助手 does, with the recognizer this app
already trusts: record the utterance (from sound over -40 dB to 1.2 s of quiet),
send it to the engine's SenseVoice through speech/transcribe — the same call
语音输入 makes — and match the text it returns. No stream, no state to get stuck
in, and 实时字幕's model is no longer a precondition for listening.
